ryx","derivation":"from G2784 (κηρύσσω);","strongs_def":" a herald, i.e. of divine truth (especially of the gospel)","kjv_def":"preacher","n":3,"o":"1TI2:7 2TI1:11 2PE2:5"},"G2755":{"lemma":"κενόδοξος","translit":"kenódoxos","derivation":"from G2756 (κενός) and G1391 (δόξα);","strongs_def":" vainly glorifying, i.e. self-conceited","kjv_def":"desirous of vain-glory","n":1,"o":"GAL5:26"},"G2736":{"lemma":"κάτω","translit":"kátō","derivation":"(compare G2737 (κατώτερος)); adverb from G2596 (κατά);","strongs_def":" downwards","kjv_def":"beneath, bottom, down, under","n":11,"o":"MAT2:16 MAT4:6 MAT27:51 MRK14:66 MRK15:38 LUK4:9 JHN8:6 JHN8:8 JHN8:23 ACT2:19 ACT20:9"},"G2762":{"lemma":"κεραία","translit":"keraía","derivation":"feminine of a presumed derivative of the base of G2768 (κέρας);","strongs_def":" something horn-like, i.e. (specially) the apex of a Hebrew letter (figuratively, the least particle)","kjv_def":"tittle","n":2,"o":"MAT5:18 LUK16:17"},"G2730":{"lemma":"κατοικέω","translit":"katoikéō","derivation":"from G2596 (κατά) and G3611 (οἰκέω);","strongs_def":" to house permanently, i.e. reside (literally or figuratively)","kjv_def":"dwell(-er), inhabitant(-ter)","n":43,"o":"MAT2:23 MAT4:13 MAT12:45 MAT23:21 LUK11:26 LUK13:4 ACT1:19 ACT1:20 ACT2:5 ACT2:9 ACT2:14 ACT4:16 ACT7:2 ACT7:4 ACT7:48 ACT9:22 ACT9:32 ACT9:35 ACT11:29 ACT13:27 ACT17:24 ACT17:26 ACT19:10 ACT19:17 ACT22:12 EPH3:17 COL1:19 COL2:9 HEB11:9 JAS4:5 2PE3:13 REV2:13 REV3:10 REV6:10 REV8:13 REV11:10 REV12:12 REV13:8 REV13:12 REV13:14 REV14:6 REV17:2 REV17:8"},"G2791":{"lemma":"Κιλικία","translit":"Kilikía","derivation":"probably of foreign origin;","strongs_def":" Cilicia, a region of Asia Minor","kjv_def":"Cilicia","n":8,"o":"ACT6:9 ACT15:23 ACT15:41 ACT21:39 ACT22:3 ACT23:34 ACT27:5 GAL1:21"},"G2735":{"lemma":"κατόρθωμα","translit":"katórthōma","derivation":"from a compound of G2596 (κατά) and a derivative of G3717 (ὀρθός) (compare G1357 (διόρθωσις));","strongs_def":" something made fully upright, i